---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page title="Resume - Josh Symonds">
  <div class="resume">
    <header class="resume-header">
      <h1>Josh Symonds</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Hands-on staff engineer: agent platforms, evals and verification, and AI infrastructure.</p>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <span class="pill">Santa Barbara, CA</span>
        <a class="pill" href="mailto:josh@joshsymonds.com">josh@joshsymonds.com</a>
        <span class="pill">+1-773-480-4810</span>
        <a class="pill" href="https://github.com/joshsymonds">github.com/joshsymonds</a>
        <a class="pill pill-download" href="/joshsymonds_resume.pdf">Download PDF</a>
      </div>
      <p class="summary">Built a company-wide agent platform and replay evals that moved its review to open-weight models, plus a decider model that replaced LLM-as-judge. Building by directing coding agents since 2025; fifteen years in infrastructure and security.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>Attain</h3>
          <span class="location">Remote</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Director of SRE, Consumer Product</span>
          <span class="tenure">Mar 2026 &ndash; Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Marvin:</strong> Created Marvin, our company-wide agent platform in Slack; 116 people across engineering, support, and operations use it for code review, incident investigation, and internal workflows, about 50 of them weekly.</li>
          <li><strong>Orchestration &amp; Gateway:</strong> Designed Go/Kubernetes orchestration for ephemeral agent workers on a Nix-built image, with per-user OAuth credentials, Cedar tool policies, and versioned model routes with one-step rollback. Launched the company&rsquo;s LLM gateway: SSO-issued keys, request logs, per-person spend, and zero-retention providers only.</li>
          <li><strong>Code Review:</strong> Shipped multi-stage AI code review with a verifier pass that checks findings and drops nitpicks: 2,100+ reviews, 87% positive (300+ ratings).</li>
          <li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Built an evaluation harness that replays production reviews against candidate models, with frozen dev/holdout cases and a version-pinned LLM judge. Blind review found the original verifier wrong on 37% of disputed calls. Moved review to open-weight models; with pipeline changes, cost per review fell 16&times; in a month and median review time halved.</li>
          <li><strong>Incidents:</strong> Automated investigation of 2,170+ alert threads, gathering evidence from kubectl, BigQuery, and logs before escalating or opening a merge request with the fix, mergeable as written 95% of the time.</li>
          <li><strong>Agent-Ready Monorepo:</strong> Made a large monorepo agent-ready with docs, agent skills, and on-demand context, shared by Marvin and engineers&rsquo; own Claude Code sessions.</li>
          <li><strong>Hiring:</strong> Designed Attain&rsquo;s AI-assisted SRE take-home interview, where candidates work on a real cloud machine with a coding agent and are graded mainly on how they work with it.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Independent Engineering, Built with Coding Agents</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3><a href="https://savecraft.gg">Savecraft</a></h3>
          <span class="location">Go, TypeScript, Rust, WebAssembly, MCP &middot; 2026</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Shipped an AI gaming companion for 14 games, in OpenAI&rsquo;s connector directory: sandboxed WASM save parsers on the player&rsquo;s device, so raw saves never leave it, and MCP tools and the chat loop on Cloudflare Workers behind OAuth 2.1.</li>
          <li>Built its eval system before choosing a model: 295 scenarios &times; 3 runs from production logs. A 13-model bake-off ranked an open-weight model first, ahead of frontier models costing 14&times; more. Replaced LLM-as-judge with a decider model (Jev) validated on held-out pairs, which picked the stronger model in 95% of pairs vs 88% for the old judge (p = 1.9e-17).</li>
          <li>Built a Go service pooling warm LuaJIT processes so agents can test builds against <a href="/blog/path-of-building-doesnt-fit/">Path of Building&rsquo;s calculation engine</a> (40 ms median).</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3><a href="https://github.com/joshsymonds/gambit">Gambit</a> &amp; Tiltyard</h3>
          <span class="location">Claude Code, Go</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Released Gambit, a Claude Code plugin that takes tasks from spec to release with test-evidence gates. Tiltyard replays real repository tasks to score models and agent harnesses.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>LiveWorld (consulting)</h3>
          <span class="location">AWS, EKS, Terraform, Flux &middot; 2013 &ndash; Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Run its AWS/EKS platform and GPU inference for its ML product (Karpenter, KEDA); wrote its SOC 2/GDPR controls.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>Open Source</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="project-desc">Original author of <a href="https://rubygems.org/gems/dynamoid">Dynamoid</a>, the Ruby ORM for DynamoDB (13M+ downloads). <a href="https://github.com/joshsymonds/nix-config">nix-config</a>: NixOS and Home Manager for a nine-host fleet (837 stars).</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Previous Roles</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>CrossnoKaye</h3>
          <span class="location">Santa Barbara, CA</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Principal Infrastructure Engineer / Senior Manager, Core Services</span>
          <span class="tenure">Jan 2021 &ndash; Feb 2026</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Platform:</strong> Built the control plane and deploy tool (approval-gated, about 5,800 deploys in 2025), the end-to-end test framework, and the CLIs; ran 9 AWS accounts and 10 EKS clusters.</li>
          <li><strong>Edge:</strong> Built the industrial IoT edge OS with zero-touch provisioning and over-the-air updates, and led the migration from k3os to Talos Linux as the fleet grew to 123 production deployments.</li>
          <li><strong>Security &amp; AI:</strong> Led SOC 2 Type 1 and presented an <a href="https://naturalrefrigerationreview.com/cybersecurity-in-automated-industrial-systems/">IIAR paper on industrial cybersecurity</a>. Set the LLM usage policy, ran weekly &ldquo;Cooking with Claude Code&rdquo; workshops, and stood up self-hosted LLM inference for internal search.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>Capital Markets Gateway</h3>
          <span class="location">Chicago, IL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">DevOps Engineer &amp; CISO</span>
          <span class="tenure">Oct 2019 &ndash; Dec 2020</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Wrote Kubernetes operators and set up multi-region failover on AKS, wrote custom Terraform providers, and ran the NIST CSF and ISO 27001 programs that passed bank audits.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>M1 Finance</h3>
          <span class="location">Chicago, IL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Chief Information Security Officer</span>
          <span class="tenure">Aug 2015 &ndash; Oct 2019</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Employee #8. Built M1&rsquo;s infrastructure from launch to nearly $1B in assets (Chef, then self-run Kubernetes, then EKS) and ran security through SOC 2 and SEC, FINRA, and bank audits.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Education</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>University of Chicago</h3>
          <span class="location">Chicago, IL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">BA in East Asian Languages and Civilizations</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <p class="pdf-link">
      <a href="/joshsymonds_resume.pdf">Download PDF version</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>

<style>
  .resume {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .resume-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .resume-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--black);
  }

  .contact-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    border: 2px solid var(--black);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    transition: box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  a.pill:hover {
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--black);
  }

  .pill-download {
    background: var(--coral);
    color: white;
    border: 2px solid var(--black);
  }

  .pill-download:hover {
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--black);
  }

  .tagline {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .summary {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: var(--space-md) auto 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .section h2 {
    color: var(--teal);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--black);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .section h2::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    right: -1.5rem;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%) rotate(45deg);
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--yellow);
    border: 2px solid var(--black);
  }

  .job {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .job-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .job-header h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--teal);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .job-header h3::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: -1rem;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--coral);
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--black);
  }

  .location {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .job-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .job-meta .title {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .tenure {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  .project-desc {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .job ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .job ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .job ul li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--teal);
  }

  .pdf-link {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .pdf-link a {
    color: var(--coral);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    font-weight: 700;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .pdf-link a:hover {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .pdf-link a::after {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--pink);
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
    vertical-align: middle;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--black);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .resume {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }

    .job-header, .job-meta {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.125rem;
    }

    .contact-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .pill {
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
